adjudicated (each is a decision with a written reason):
  idempotency_records.response_status
    CLOSED by migration 0020, triggers trg_idempotency_completed_requires_status and its _update twin. A CHECK cannot express this: the `completed` arm's `BETWEEN` is NULL and the pending arm's `IS NULL` is conjoined with other conditions, so no arm is a pure nullness test. A trigger is NULL-safe and additive, so the table was not rebuilt and rollback stays a Worker rollback. Proven by the p07 case `a completed record with NO status is refused`.

no nullable column is compared with BETWEEN anywhere NULL would let the whole
CHECK pass. `idempotency_records.response_status` was the only one; migration
0020 closes it and a probe in p07-schema-invariants.mjs proves it.
